EtherCAT/Pci1203LinkWatch.h (new, header-only, pure): the decision. Signal = what the read-only monitor
already samples every Poll -- each scanned station's Acm_DevGetSlaveStates (down = read failed or not
EC_SLAVE_STATE_OP, golden MyEtherCAT.cpp:531's strict OP), the monitor's self-disable (card not answering),
card().open false, an empty scan / a re-learnt ring with nothing in OP. No new vendor call;
pci1203_readonly_gate PASS. Arms only after the link was up once (open, not disabled, a station in OP), so
the initial open / cold-boot scan / a never-linked build never alarm. Stations are watched once seen in OP;
unaddressable twins skipped; a changed scan (Refresh) re-learns the ring. First lost sample starts the timer;
kPci1203LinkLostAlarmMs (10000, the one place) of continuous loss -> kAlarm ONCE with the reason (signal,
since when, per-ring tally, first stations not in OP; CSV/quote safe, <= 400 bytes); one UP sample resets.

tools/wb_serve.cpp: after both Poll() sites (main IO clock; native-forms drag keepalive) one call to
W906_Pci1203LinkWatchTick (EOF). On kAlarm it calls golden's own ShowErrorMessage(WAR16152, 0, MMSystem,
0, reason) (golden MyEtherCAT.cpp:333): the existing kcode==0 notice path -- StopAllMotor + SoftStop/
SoftStart/SystemStart=false + 1203 DecStop (W906_AlarmStopLikeGolden), the golden alarm record, the popup
notice. No card re-open (golden's OpenEtherCatMastCard after WAR16152 is not done). stdout + oplog LINK lines.

tests/test_pci1203_linkwatch.cpp + tests/CMakeLists.txt (ctest Pci1203LinkWatch, built like Pci1203Pure):
fake monitor + fake clock, 43 checks (9.9 s none / 10 s one / still lost none / restored reset / again /
never linked / card-level signals / tick wrap); 5 mutations of the watch all caught.

